From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:33:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [ppc64] smith: add the ppc64 architecture; map a ppc64le host
 to it

pkg/test_runner could not start on a ppc64le host: smith's
Architecture.host runs `uname -m` and throws "Unknown host architecture:
ppc64le", and test_runner evaluates it while building its option parser
(the --arch default), so even `-a simarm64` runs died at startup.

Adds Architecture.ppc64 and maps uname "ppc64le" to it. Every switch over
Architecture in test_runner already has a default arm.

Class: needed locally to run tools/test.py-style suites on this host;
upstreamable only together with the ppc64 backend.
---
 pkg/smith/lib/configuration.dart | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/smith/lib/configuration.dart b/pkg/smith/lib/configuration.dart
index 9398ac21..203cc76c 100644
--- a/pkg/smith/lib/configuration.dart
+++ b/pkg/smith/lib/configuration.dart
@@ -736,7 +736,8 @@ enum Architecture {
   riscv32._('riscv32'),
   riscv64._('riscv64'),
   simriscv32._('simriscv32', isSimulator: true),
-  simriscv64._('simriscv64', isSimulator: true);
+  simriscv64._('simriscv64', isSimulator: true),
+  ppc64._('ppc64');
 
   final String name;
   final bool isSimulator;
@@ -801,6 +802,9 @@ enum Architecture {
         return riscv32;
       case "riscv64":
         return riscv64;
+      // Little-endian only; "ppc64" from uname is big-endian.
+      case "ppc64le":
+        return ppc64;
     }
 
     throw "Unknown host architecture: $arch";
